# The developer-facing surfaces and the pages under apps/docs that describe each one (ADR 0088).
# PR / pr docs (scripts/ci/pr-docs.mjs) reads this file from the pull request's checkout: when a
# pull request changes a file under a surface and its Docs section says none, the reason must name
# the surface. The code-reviewer agent reads the pages of each surface the diff touches before the
# pull request opens. test/meta/docs-paths.test.ts keeps the file in step with the folders: every
# pattern matches a tracked file, every page exists, and every surface below has an entry.
#
# An entry is a pattern in the syntax of .github/risk-paths (a leading slash anchors it at the root,
# a pattern that names a folder covers everything below it), then the pages that describe the
# surface, separated by spaces, or "none yet" while the surface has no page. A page lives under
# apps/docs; a file under docs/ describes a decision, not the product, and is no page. The screens
# and the use guides are not mapped: user guides come in one docs task per epic (ADR 0049), and the
# screenshots are regenerated before each release.

# The HTTP surface: the public REST API, its credentials and rate limits, the trusted proxy and the
# web origins. The install guide describes the rate limits; the REST, authentication and errors
# pages of the Integrate group are not written yet.
